#!/usr/local/bin/vmd
# 073.BondedStages - visualization of stage 2 (the fully refined model)
#
# stage2.nc.pdb carries CONECT records for every spring (see --pdbconect in
# the Makefile). Stage 3 is shown because it has the most to look at; swap
# the filename for stage1/stage2 to see how little the drawn network itself
# changes between stages -- what changes is each spring's equilibrium and
# stiffness, plus the ghost particles the dihedral model adds, not which
# real atoms are connected. Loaded with filebonds 1, autobonds 0
# so every bond drawn is exactly one of those springs -- nothing guessed
# from interatomic distances, nothing missing.
#
# Two representations on the same "all" selection:
#   - CPK: the classic ball-and-stick view of the structure.
#   - Bonds: a thin orange overlay highlighting the spring network itself,
#     including the non-covalent 1-3/1-4 rigidifying springs (e.g. the
#     N...C distance inside a residue's CA tetrahedron) that a plain
#     ball-and-stick rendering of real chemistry would not show.

mol new stage2.nc.pdb type pdb first 0 last -1 step 1 filebonds 1 autobonds 0 waitfor all
mol delrep 0 top

mol representation CPK 0.6 0.2 12.0 12.0
mol color Name
mol selection {all}
mol material Opaque
mol addrep top

mol representation Bonds 0.08 12.0
mol color ColorID 3
mol selection {all}
mol material Opaque
mol addrep top

mol rename top ubiquitin

display projection Orthographic
display depthcue off
display rendermode GLSL
color Display Background white
axes location off

menu imd on
imd transfer 1000
imd connect localhost 3000
